------------------------------------------------------------------------
Prior art
------------------------------------------------------------------------

Vending-machine agent benchmarking is prior art, and this implementation's
per-product economics follow a shape established in that literature: a
reference price, a base sales rate at that price, and a price elasticity per
item. Everything here is independently written and independently parameterised.
No score produced by this benchmark is comparable with a score from any other
vending benchmark.

------------------------------------------------------------------------
Third-party components
------------------------------------------------------------------------

The simulation server and the benchmark scripts use only the Python 3.11+
standard library at runtime, apart from the MCP transport. Optional and
development dependencies, none of which are vendored or redistributed here,
are all permissively licensed:

  fastmcp ........ Apache-2.0 .... https://github.com/jlowin/fastmcp
  httpx .......... BSD-3-Clause .. https://github.com/encode/httpx
  python-dotenv .. BSD-3-Clause .. https://github.com/theskumar/python-dotenv
  pytest ......... MIT ........... https://github.com/pytest-dev/pytest
  matplotlib ..... PSF-based ..... https://github.com/matplotlib/matplotlib
  uv ............. Apache-2.0/MIT  https://github.com/astral-sh/uv

Model runs are executed by invoking the user's own authenticated Claude CLI or
the user's own OpenRouter account. Neither is bundled or redistributed, and no
API credentials are stored in this repository or in its published results.

Supplier companies, products, customers, email addresses, prices and locations
in the simulation are fictional. Any resemblance to real businesses is
coincidental. The economy is synthetic and is not fitted to real point-of-sale
data.

